;; Lifecycle: permanent library, part of the language built on the kernel.
;;
;; The memory of a program: one, which every module shares. A module
;; takes it from a module it requires with (memory from name), down to
;; this one, which defines it (spec 3.3) and holds nothing of its own:
;; print.sub keeps its bytes at 0..1023, and the C language's heap and
;; stack (next/c/lang.sub) lie above every module's data. It grows as
;; the program needs (memory.grow, from lang.sub's sbrk).

(memory 1)
